OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1793847325
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AUK commits to 'time-bound' talks on
OL,4,Aslavery apology
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe 18 page document includes a
OL,7,Fparagraph in which the leaders "welcome
OL,8,Fthe agreement of the Government of the
OL,9,FUnited Kingdom to engage in a
OL,10,Fstructured, time-bound, inclusive and
OL,11,Fgood-faith dialogue with affected
OL,12,Fparties addressing the transatlantic
OL,13,Ftrafficking of enslaved Africans and
OL,14,Fits historical harms".
OL,16,FIt comes after Prime Minister Andy
OL,17,FBurnham opened the door to a formal
OL,18,Fapology on behalf of the UK for its
OL,19,Frole in the slave trade, while ruling
OL,20,Fout the prospect of reparations.
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
